Today’s Daily Brief with James Bowater, Founder of The Digital Commonwealth & Chair of Roundtable Wednesdays 

Tuesday 13th October September 2026

Headlines:

(1) A Chinese Memory Chip Advance Sends the Kospi Down More Than 7 Percent and Rattles the AI Trade; 
(2) Houthi Strikes Keep Riyadh Airport Shut as Britain Accuses Iran's Revolutionary Guard of Directing the RAF Fairford Plot; 
(3) Wall Street Closes Mixed Ahead of the First Bank Earnings of the Season and Wednesday's CPI Report; 
(4) Bitcoin Falls Below $82,000 and $771 Million of Leveraged Positions Are Liquidated; 
(5) South Korea Moves to Block 27 Unregistered Crypto Exchanges as Kraken Wins Full Dubai Approval; 
(6) The EU Adopts Its Largest Sanctions Listings Since 2022 Against Almost 1,600 Russian Military Suppliers; 
(7) The IMF Lifts Its Global Growth Forecast to 3.1 Percent as the Fed's Hammack Says Rates Must Rise Further; 
(8) Meta Unveils Its Wonder Models and Morgan Stanley Pushes Tokenised Equities Support to the First Quarter of 2027.

Crypto: 
Bitcoin is trading around $81,400 to $82,000 on Tuesday, down about 2 to 3 percent over 24 hours, after breaking below the $82,000 support level from Monday's high of about $84,200, with CoinGlass recording about $771 million of liquidations over 24 hours, of which $685.6 million were long positions. Ether is trading near $2,425 to $2,460, down 4 to 5 percent, XRP trades near $1.33 to $1.37, Solana near $103 to $105 and Dogecoin near $0.082

Institutional: 
JPMorgan, Goldman Sachs, Wells Fargo and Citigroup Open the Bank Earnings Season Today, While Strategy Adds 250 Bitcoin and Repurchases $192 Million of STRC, Monte dei Paschi Pushes Back on Intesa's Raised Offer and Telia Plans to Cut About 900 Jobs

Regulatory: 
South Korea Moves to Block 27 Unregistered Crypto Exchanges Including KuCoin and MEXC, While the EU Adopts Its Largest Sanctions Listings Since 2022, Kraken Wins Full Dubai Approval and Australia Weighs Leverage Caps for Crypto Settled Derivatives

Stablecoin: 
Morgan Stanley now sees the first quarter of 2027 as a more realistic timeline for supporting tokenised equities on its alternative trading system, later than the second half of 2026 that Amy Oldenburg, its head of digital asset strategy, had indicated in March, according to an interview with The Block at Token2049 

Technology: 
Meta Unveils Its Wonder and Wonder Full Models and Says They Rival OpenAI and Anthropic, While Aptos Launches an Encrypted Mempool and OneKey Cuts CryptoBilis as the Ledger Supply Chain Inquiry Widens

Other Stories: 
SpaceX Is Due to Launch the CRS 35 Cargo Mission With the Final Pair of ISS Roll Out Solar Arrays

